      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "WORCESTER (8) is the one to beat after a sound fourth behind Olden in a BM54+ at Northam, where he was at long odds but stayed on well enough to suggest this BM64+ is within reach. The rise in grade is the query, but his recent effort stacks up and can land the knockout blow. ICANDOIT ONMYOWN (4) has a more volatile last-start figure after finishing last over 2200m at Northam, but her second to Olden the run prior reads well for this and she has already had WORCESTER covered in that form line. LAND OF FIRE (5) brings the freshest winning form, having beaten QUEEN NARDI at Moora in a BM56+ despite racing keenly and wide from the 800m. The untried 1990m asks more of him, but he is race fit and the winning rider stays on. QUEEN NARDI (2) was honest behind LAND OF FIRE first-up and gets a 3kg claim, so she appeals as the most reliable place profile if she handles the stronger grade. MACHO ARQUERO (6) can improve on the fresh effort.",
